{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Eagles collection feels like a natural next choice because I have been choosing familiar classic rock and hits collections, including The Cars and Now Classic Rock Hits.",
    "Carole King’s Tapestry appeals through melodic songwriting that connects with my interest in Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie, while Frankie Valli fits my interest in mid-sixties pop."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Shania Twain’s collection shares the greatest-hits format, but country pop is less appealing to me right now than older pop and classic rock.",
    "I cannot choose The Complete Hit Singles or The Complete Greatest Hits confidently because I do not know the artists; the titles alone do not establish a musical connection."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in greatest-hits collections seems to have been treated as a reason to recommend almost any collection, although the artist and musical style matter more.",
    "An older era or classic-rock connection makes something worth considering, but it does not make every related release an equally strong choice today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My interest in Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie points toward melodic songwriting as well as familiar hits, which is why Tapestry stands out.",
    "I choose selectively: the Eagles and Tapestry appeal enough to pick now, while Pat Benatar, Heart, and other plausible matches are lower priorities, and The Real 70’S depends on its track list."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in older pop and classic rock, but put too much weight on compilation titles and too little on the specific music I want today."
}"}
